{{!--
  cover-letter.md.hbs — renders one prepared cover letter (mvp-spec §3 F7).
  Same claim-citation contract as resume.md.hbs: every sentence the model
  writes carries the claim label(s) it cites, and the validator refuses one
  that doesn't (mvp-spec F7: "rejects any sentence that cites no confirmed
  claim ID"). The runner's exporter renders this template, then strips the
  citation markers.

  The date, greeting and sign-off are the runner's, not the model's, so
  there is no uncited "connective" sentence: the greeting names the company
  only when its extracted name reads as a plain name (runner/export/
  document.ts, plainCompanyName), and says "Dear hiring team," otherwise.

  Render context (runner/export/document.ts, CoverLetterModel):
    {
      person: { name, contact },  // see resume.md.hbs — typed by the person
      date: string,                // the date this was prepared, written out:
                                   // "September 24, 2026"
      greeting: string,            // "Dear Northwind Labs hiring team,"
      paragraphs: [
        {
          statements: [
            { text: string, claimIds: [string, ...] } // never empty
          ]
        }
      ],
      signOff: string              // "Sincerely,"
    }
--}}
{{date}}

{{greeting}}

{{#each paragraphs}}
{{#each this.statements}}{{this.text}}{{#each this.claimIds}} `[{{this}}]`{{/each}} {{/each}}

{{/each}}
{{signOff}}

{{person.name}}
{{#if person.contact}}
{{person.contact}}
{{/if}}
